---
// Static privacy notice, linked from the footer in BaseLayout.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<title>Privacy | MCU Chronological Watchlist</title>
		<meta name="description" content="What mcu.watch stores about you and why." />
	</Fragment>

	<article class="privacy">
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="updated">Last updated: 13 September 2026</p>

		<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
		<p>
			mcu.watch is a fan project run by Amber van den Berg. Questions about your data go to{' '}
			<a href="mailto:info@mcu.watch">info@mcu.watch</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>What is stored and why</h2>
		<p>When you sign in, the site stores:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Your email address, to send you a login link and to know which progress is yours.</li>
			<li>What you marked as watched or skipped, so you can pick up where you left off.</li>
			<li>A login cookie that keeps you signed in for 60 days.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			For every visitor, the server logs requests without your IP address, to find errors. These logs are kept for 30
			days.
		</p>
		<p>Legal basis: your account. For server logs: keeping the site working.</p>
		<p>Your email address and progress stay until you ask to delete them.</p>

		<h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Microsoft Azure hosts the site and stores the data in the Netherlands.</li>
			<li>Resend sends the login email and stores your email address in the US.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Both are US companies.</p>

		<h2>Other websites</h2>
		<p>
			Posters load from Amazon and trailer images load from YouTube, so your browser sends your IP address to those
			servers. Trailers load from YouTube or IMDb only after you click, and they may set cookies then.
		</p>

		<h2>Your rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can ask to see, correct, export or delete your data, or object to how it is used. Email&nbsp;
			<a href="mailto:info@mcu.watch">info@mcu.watch</a>. Not happy with how your data is handled? You can file a
			complaint with&nbsp;
			<a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
				Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens
			</a>
			&nbsp;(the Dutch data protection authority).
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.privacy {
		width: min(820px, 100%);
		margin: 0 auto;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	h2 {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		font-size: 1.2rem;
	}

	h1,
	.updated {
		text-align: center;
	}

	.updated {
		color: var(--muted);
	}
</style>
